# Claude Code (CLI) — Complete Cheat Sheet (Single-Page Doc)

---

## 1) Basic Usage

### Start Interactive Mode

```bash
claude
```

### One-Off Prompt (Non-Interactive)

```bash
claude -p "Explain what this repo does and how to run it"
```

### Specify Files Explicitly (Best Practice)

```bash
claude -p "Review and improve these files: src/app.py README.md"
```

### Use Specific Model

```bash
claude --model <model-name>
```

### Resume Previous Session (If Supported)

```bash
claude --resume
```

---

## 2) Repo Understanding Prompts

### Understand a Codebase Quickly

```text
Scan this repository and produce:
1) What it does
2) How to run locally
3) Key modules and flow
4) Risks or technical debt
5) 5 quick improvement ideas
Keep it concise and structured.
```

### Architecture Summary

```text
Summarize the architecture:
- Entry point
- Core services
- Data flow
- External dependencies
- Risks
Keep it technical and precise.
```

---

## 3) Feature Development Prompts

### Add a Feature (Safe Mode)

```text
Implement feature: <FEATURE>

Constraints:
- Minimal diff
- Do not break existing behavior
- No new dependencies
- Add tests
- Update README

Show implementation plan first.
```

### Refactor Safely

```text
Refactor <MODULE> for readability and maintainability.

Rules:
- No behavior change
- Keep public APIs stable
- Follow existing patterns
- Add or update tests
Explain key decisions briefly.
```

---

## 4) Debugging Prompts

### Diagnose an Error

```text
I am seeing this error:

<PASTE ERROR>

1) Identify root cause
2) Propose 2 possible fixes
3) Implement safest fix
4) Add regression test
```

### Performance Issue

```text
Investigate performance issue in <MODULE>.
- Identify bottlenecks
- Suggest measurable improvements
- Avoid premature optimization
```

